the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base overlaps includes these resources:
    lomo.

the knowledge base overlaps includes:

the text of the source description is at "sources/overlaps.ttl".

% Who bears a duty: the agent of this role of the action (lomo.le).
the bearer role is addresser.


action project a is identified by "http://example.org/Action_ProjectA".

action project a is an action.

action project a has the time specification action project a time.


action project a time is a temporal specification.

action project a time has the instant 2025-01-01.

action project a time has the duration "P6M".


action project b is identified by "http://example.org/Action_ProjectB".

action project b is an action.

action project b has the time specification action project b time.


action project b time is a temporal specification.

action project b time has the instant 2025-03-01.

action project b time has the duration "P6M".


temporal spec project a is identified by "http://example.org/TemporalSpec_ProjectA".

temporal spec project a overlaps temporal spec project b.


temporal spec event a is identified by "http://example.org/TemporalSpec_EventA".

temporal spec event a is a temporal specification.

temporal spec event a has the instant 2025-01-01.

temporal spec event a has the duration "P3M".

temporal spec event a overlaps temporal spec event b.


temporal spec event b is identified by "http://example.org/TemporalSpec_EventB".

temporal spec event b is a temporal specification.

temporal spec event b has the instant 2025-02-01.

temporal spec event b has the duration "P3M".


% Things the description names but does not describe: their addresses.
temporal spec project b is identified by "http://example.org/TemporalSpec_ProjectB".


% The questions of LOMO's requirements document (its competency questions),
% as far as a description can answer them.
scenario the_periods is, as stated in the source description:
    first_dates expects answers ["the first date of action project a time is 2025-01-01", "the first date of action project b time is 2025-03-01", "the first date of temporal spec event a is 2025-01-01", "the first date of temporal spec event b is 2025-02-01"].
    last_dates expects answers ["the last date of action project a time is 2025-07-01", "the last date of action project b time is 2025-09-01", "the last date of temporal spec event a is 2025-04-01", "the last date of temporal spec event b is 2025-05-01"].
    broken_links expects answers [].

query applies is:
    which rule applies to which party.

query rules_without_conditions is:
    which rule has no written conditions.

query kinds is:
    which thing is of the kind which kind.

query prescriptive is:
    which thing is a prescriptive rule.

query constitutive is:
    which thing is a constitutive rule.

query durations is:
    which temporal specification has the duration which duration.

query instants is:
    which temporal specification has the instant which date.

query overlaps is:
    which temporal specification overlaps which second temporal specification.

query first_dates is:
    the first date of which temporal specification is which date.

query last_dates is:
    the last date of which temporal specification is which date.

query later_times is:
    which temporal specification is later than which second temporal specification.

query times_within is:
    which temporal specification is during which second temporal specification.

query broken_links is:
    which temporal specification breaks its link with which second temporal specification.

query hours_as_days is:
    which temporal specification has a length of time that counts hours as whole days.

query parts is:
    which thing is part of the description.

query texts is:
    which thing is described by the text which text.

query addresses is:
    which thing is identified by which address.

query bearer is:
    the bearer role is which role.

